itar project/PDF version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_7_Three_String_Skip_Relay.pdf","sha256":"5c8607cff40801acb13f5e08dd2988b2ff943593eb084de2801f05f507a6c4ea","text":"108 Finger Permutations - Level 7\nThree-String Skip Relay: 1+2+1 Double-Gap Crossing Control\nLevel 7 combines the three-string relay from Level 4 with the skipped-string landings developed in Levels 5 and 6.\n1. Keep the foundation fixed\n1 = index / fret 5\n2 = middle / fret 6\n3 = ring / fret 7\n4 = pinky / fret 8\nThe four-digit code never changes.\n2. Relay across every other string\nAscend: E-D-B, then A-G-e.\nDescend: e-G-A, then B-D-E.\nNote 1 starts; notes 2-3 share the middle.\nNote 4 completes the second gap crossing.\n3. Make both gaps inaudible\nBoth intervening strings stay silent.\nFirst pass: accent landing notes 2 and 4.\nSecond pass: equalize all four notes.\nUse both downstroke and upstroke starts.\nWorked example - code 1234\nPlay 1 on the first string, 2-3 on the next played string, and 4 on the third; one silent string separates each landing.\nASCEND - E-D-B / A-G-e\nDESCEND - e-G-A / B-D-E\ne|--------|------8-|\nB|------8-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-7---|\nD|--6-7---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-7---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-7---|\nA|------8-|--------|\nE|--------|------8-|\nPASS 1\nSeparate the four-note cells; lightly accent notes 2 and 4 and audit both silent strings.\nPASS 2\nConnect the route, remove the accents, and keep volume, timing, and note length even.\nMove diagonally with shallow pick depth; do not turn either gap into a large vertical jump.\nPractice protocol\n1\nChoose one 12-exercise set.\n2\nStart 10-15 BPM below the slower\nof your clean Level 6 modes.\n3\nPlay every exercise up and down\nwith a downstroke start.\n4\nRepeat the full set with an\nupstroke start.\n5\nAfter three clean loops, add\n2 BPM next session.\n6\nAfter two noisy gaps or tension,\nreduce 4-6 BPM; require two clean days.\nStandard tuning. Fifth position. 1+2+1 across three played strings; clear one silent string at each crossing.\nPage 1 of 10\n","text_sha256":"3e405140696f90a02abf6288650e0ca7232eefb7fa839f7a8ea8d773ab59c775"},"L7-PDF1-p2":{"format":"pdf","page":2,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_7_Three_String_Skip_Relay.pdf","sha256":"5c8607cff40801acb13f5e08dd2988b2ff943593eb084de2801f05f507a6c4ea","text":"Level 7 - Three-String Skip Relay\nSet 1 of 9 - Exercises 001-012\n1+2+1: notes 2 and 4 land across separate silent strings; preserve the four-digit code order.\n001   1212\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------6-|\nB|------6-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-5---|\nD|--6-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-5---|\nA|------6-|--------|\nE|--------|------6-|\n002   1213\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------7-|\nB|------7-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-5---|\nD|--6-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-5---|\nA|------7-|--------|\nE|--------|------7-|\n003   1214\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------8-|\nB|------8-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-5---|\nD|--6-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-5---|\nA|------8-|--------|\nE|--------|------8-|\n004   1231\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------5-|\nB|------5-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-7---|\nD|--6-7---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-7---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-7---|\nA|------5-|--------|\nE|--------|------5-|\n005   1232\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------6-|\nB|------6-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-7---|\nD|--6-7---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-7---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-7---|\nA|------6-|--------|\nE|--------|------6-|\n006   1234\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------8-|\nB|------8-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-7---|\nD|--6-7---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-7---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-7---|\nA|------8-|--------|\nE|--------|------8-|\n007   1241\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------5-|\nB|------5-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-8---|\nD|--6-8---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-8---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-8---|\nA|------5-|--------|\nE|--------|------5-|\n008   1242\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------6-|\nB|------6-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-8---|\nD|--6-8---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-8---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-8---|\nA|------6-|--------|\nE|--------|------6-|\n009   1243\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------7-|\nB|------7-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-8---|\nD|--6-8---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-8---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-8---|\nA|------7-|--------|\nE|--------|------7-|\n010   1312\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------6-|\nB|------6-|--------|\nG|--------|--7-5---|\nD|--7-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--7-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--7-5---|\nA|------6-|--------|\nE|--------|------6-|\n011   1313\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------7-|\nB|------7-|--------|\nG|--------|--7-5---|\nD|--7-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--7-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--7-5---|\nA|------7-|--------|\nE|--------|------7-|\n012   1314\n1+2+1 SKIP RELAY\nUP\ne|--------|------8-|\nB|------8-|--------|\nG|--------|--7-5---|\nD|--7-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDN\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--7-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--7-5---|\nA|------8-|--------|\nE|--------|------8-|\nStandard tuning. Fifth position. 1+2+1 across three played strings; clear one silent string at each crossing.\nPage 2 of 10\n","text_sha256":"aebe20a0651f5b638f95f28af59268a47264d55e24ab0b1e55e0385cd692b8f5"},"L7-TXT1-1-24":{"first_line":1,"format":"txt","last_line":24,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_7_Three_String_Skip_Relay.txt","sha256":"467d1401237e34633efc4c517fa98d8190f0b47346a7b34be9d2548924883b61","text":"108 FINGER PERMUTATIONS - LEVEL 7: THREE-STRING SKIP RELAY\n1+2+1 double-gap crossing and muting control in standard tuning.\nFifth position: 1=index/fret 5, 2=middle/fret 6, 3=ring/fret 7, 4=pinky/fret 8.\n\nMOVEMENT RULE\nPlay code note 1 on the first played string, code notes 2-3 on the middle played string, and code note 4 on the third.\nLeave one physical string silent between the first and middle played strings and another silent string between the middle\nand third played strings. Ascend through E-D-B and A-G-e. Descend through e-G-A and B-D-E.\nThe 1+2+1 description refers to note counts, not finger numbers. The four-digit code order never changes.\n\nWHY THIS IS LEVEL 7\nLevel 4 introduced the 1+2+1 relay across adjacent strings. Levels 5 and 6 trained one skipped-string crossing at\ndifferent rhythmic points. Level 7 combines those skills: both crossings in the relay now clear a silent string.\nThis doubles the number of skipped-string landings per code without adding a position shift or a wider individual leap.\n\nPRACTICE RULE\nUse one 12-exercise set per session. Begin 10-15 BPM below the slower of your two clean Level 6 modes.\nPlay ASCEND directly into DESCEND, then repeat the entire exercise with the opposite starting pick stroke.\nFirst pass: separate the four-note cells, use short notes, and lightly accent landing notes 2 and 4.\nVerify that both intervening strings remain silent and that neither crossing becomes an exaggerated vertical jump.\nSecond pass: connect the route, remove the accents, and equalize all four notes in volume, timing, and duration.\nUse straight 16ths first. Reintroduce triplet and quintuplet groupings only after both gap landings are stable.\nAfter three clean loops, add 2 BPM next session. After two noisy gaps, errors, or rising tension, reduce 4-6 BPM.\nAdvance after the full set is clean with both pick starts on two separate days.","text_sha256":"0f6f6ba87848b155463f5a934b73b17a4055f5ccc5289541fe6610086871109b"},"L7-TXT1-30-44":{"first_line":30,"format":"txt","last_line":44,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_7_Three_String_Skip_Relay.txt","sha256":"467d1401237e34633efc4c517fa98d8190f0b47346a7b34be9d2548924883b61","text":"Exercise 001: 1212\nASCEND - E-D-B, A-G-e\ne|--------|------6-|\nB|------6-|--------|\nG|--------|--6-5---|\nD|--6-5---|--------|\nA|--------|5-------|\nE|5-------|--------|\nDESCEND - e-G-A, B-D-E\ne|5-------|--------|\nB|--------|5-------|\nG|--6-5---|--------|\nD|--------|--6-5---|\nA|------6-|--------|\nE|--------|------6-|","text_sha256":"443c0208a7b1d9c32ce6422afb3ff4562dc543e309bae2042774ce8f5534d0a0"}}},"reference_registry":{"entities":[{"id":"fg:course:000001","kind":"course","label":"Fathom Guitar105","parent":null},{"id":"fg:workbook:000007","kind":"workbook","label":"Legacy Level7","parent":"fg:course:000001"},{"id":"fg:module:001148","kind":"module","label":"Level7 Exercise001 connected Pass2 relay","parent":"fg:workbook:000007"},{"id":"fg:item:001148","kind":"item","label":"Level 7 Exercise 001 1212 connected skip relay Pass2","parent":"fg:module:001148"},{"id":"fg:variant:007418","kind":"variant","label":"ex001-connected-pass2-D-start","parent":"fg:item:001148"},{"id":"fg:variant:007419","kind":"variant","label":"ex001-connected-pass2-U-start","parent":"fg:item:001148"}],"identity_version":1,"rules":"Opaque allocated IDs never recomputed from titles, file paths, local code, position in navigation or content hash; parent edges may change only with reviewed provenance. Workbook initial allocations reflect frozen source identities, never renumber."},"resource_plan":{"availability":"required_unsupplied","entry_ids":["R39","R48","R73","R74","R75","R76","R77","R78","R79","R95","R96","R97A","R97B","R97C","R99","R105"],"path":"Results/20260906T184530Z-2.4.1.1.1-r01-evidence/plan.json","sha256":"cb3c3f7a47343ac0255dbdb8bf53411af6dd7b929c101b04d00ed62d6e3f637a"}}
